;; "As built: JN9a"). None.
;;
;; :bridges (JFS94 (b), "As built: JN9b"): the reads of arbace.repr.java.model that may answer a native object by
;; javac's symbol of the same declaration; a read bridged that is not listed fails the check. Until JN9f it listed
;; the five of JN9b-JN9d (:model/binary-name, :model/package-members, :model/type, :model/const-value,
;; :model/supertypes), which JN9e made native (none bridged in any corpus); since JN9f (JFS128 (b)) none: a bridge
;; is a gap of the read without javac, and any fails the check.
{:bridges #{}}
